  "conclusion": "Broad omission of paired physical-Pencil PAN is observably not native-modal parity: for dy=+20 the exact Circle modal changes radius 25->31 and the exact Transform PROPSIZE case changes radius 2->2.2; omitting PAN while retaining ordinary MOUSEMOVE leaves those radii 25 and 2. Circle radius is persisted by RNA_int_set. Ordinary mouse positioning still executes in both consumers. These are native advanced size semantics, not viewport navigation.",
  "policy_implication": "Do not describe a canvas-wide Pencil paired-PAN omission as navigation-only or as preserving all native advanced controls. A Knife-scoped correction can leave Circle/Transform TRACKPADPAN mappings intact; this characterization supplies no receipt, recognizer or lifecycle implementation.",
  "model_boundaries": [
    "The complete actual WM_gesture_circle_modal function executes, including mouse-motion, SIZE, ADD, persistence and min clamp. RNA property storage, apply-selection, redraw and gesture-end are explicit small instrumentation; no scene selection geometry is executed.",
    "Actual Transform PROPSIZE/UP/DOWN case bodies and actual MOUSEMOVE branch body execute. Their surrounding dispatcher, numeric-input precedence, modal poll, transformations, snapping, calculatePropRatio geometry and WM ownership are not executed. calculatePropRatio only records invocation.",
    "Actual native Python keymap functions execute for both use_alt_navigation settings. A small explicit stock-binding matcher checks type/value/modifier admission; custom keymaps and real WM dispatch are not simulated.",
    "wmEvent xy/prev_xy and native mapped action are supplied explicitly. No claim that a physical device produces this exact dy, or that all contacts reach these consumers. Modifier and proportional-edit preconditions are stated and exercised.",
    "No production overlay or existing tests changed; no new iOS build, target execution, UIKit/device proof, stock GUI input injection, binary commit, assertion weakening or rollback claim."
